          {
            "id": 2910467,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "The Isle Of Man isn't part of The United Kingdom, and it has its own parliament called Tynwald. It's claimed that this is the world's oldest parliament that's still functioning and that it dates back to September. However, the earliest surviving reference to it is from 1422, so perhaps it isn't quite as old as it claims. Day three, we have a trip to the mountain Snaefell. This begins with a leisurely ride along the promenade in Douglas in a horse drawn tram.",
